The [original #4471 page](/kb/incidents/4471) calls this one known parser issue with one fix queued.
Its rendered evidence shows two causes. Keep their tickets and fixes separate. This review uses the
2026-10-04 KB export; the review date does not mean the live support queue was refreshed.

## What the evidence supports

<IncidentReview />

## Different mechanisms, different fixes

**Shared parser:** day-first tenants supply day/month dates, but the shared parser reads month first.
For example, harbour.dental's app report `R-41200` describes 7 April becoming 4 July;
lantern.row's `R-41203` describes 2 December becoming 12 February. Fix the shared parsing contract
and verify the tenant's intended date survives. See [parser ticket](https://github.com/level44/mega.dev.challenge/issues/1).

**Form hint:** booking-v3 displays `MM/DD/YYYY`, while its day-first form reads input in the tenant's order.
Following the hint makes the user enter month/day and the form interprets day/month. This affects
form reports from alder.physio, copper.studio and pale.harbour. `R-41230`, `R-41241` and `R-41251`
are examples. Align the displayed hint with the actual form contract; a shared-parser fix alone does
not establish this is repaired. See [form-hint ticket](https://github.com/level44/mega.dev.challenge/issues/2).

These are mechanisms described by the exported executable model, not a reproduction against the
production product. The individual one-day-like reports remain explicitly uncertain above.

## What the timeline actually measures

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

The received and merged series answer different questions. Read them separately before attributing
a change in support activity to a release, the onset of a bug or a successful fix. No deployment or
recovery evidence is included in this export.

## Replace subject-only triage with evidence of the same cause

The [triage runbook](/kb/triage/dedupe) still instructs the desk to merge on normalized subjects and
merge when unsure. Its old review date triggers the layout's stale warning. An accepted label does
not make it current or make its advice agree with the running examples.

<DedupeExplorer />

Try alder.physio with the same subject on both sides: form versus app yields different causes.
Change the app side to form and the cause agrees. Conversely, kettle.books app and email can share
a cause despite different subjects. Two unknown tenants do not establish a shared cause either.
Tenant, form and channel matter; subject, browser locale and intake tag are insufficient.

**Proposed replacement rule:** read the report and establish its tenant and relevant input path.
Merge only when the evidence supports the same underlying cause; different wording or channels do
not by themselves prevent a merge. Keep different causes separate. With an unknown tenant or an
unexplained symptom, investigate instead of automatically merging.

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) remains unchanged as an accepted historical
record. This review proposes replacing its operational rule; it does not claim the original deciders
have accepted a new decision. Record a new decision if that proposal is accepted.

